---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '25 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy · Belal Zaky"
  description="How Mission Control, a personal single-user dashboard, handles bank account data accessed through Enable Banking."
>
  <article class="legal container container--prose">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-dek">
        This policy covers <strong>Mission Control</strong>, a personal desktop application I built
        and use myself. It explains what account data the application accesses, where that data is
        stored, and who can see it.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who this is</h2>
      <p>
        Mission Control is written and operated by Belal Zaky, an individual based in London, United
        Kingdom. It is not a company, a product, or a service offered to anyone else. Questions about
        this policy go to <a href="mailto:belal4606@gmail.com">belal4606@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who uses the application</h2>
      <p>
        I am the only user. There are no accounts, no sign-up, and no way for another person to
        connect their bank to this application. The only bank accounts it can reach are ones I
        personally own and have explicitly linked to it. If that ever changes — if the application is
        opened up to other people — this policy will be rewritten before that happens, not after.
      </p>

      <h2>What data is accessed</h2>
      <p>
        The application connects to my own bank through
        <a href="https://enablebanking.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Enable Banking</a>,
        a licensed account information service provider (AISP) operating under PSD2 and UK Open
        Banking rules. Through that connection it reads:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>account identifiers, names, currency and balances for the accounts I have linked;</li>
        <li>booked transactions on those accounts — date, amount, currency, description, and counterparty name.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Access is <strong>read-only</strong>. The application cannot move money, initiate payments,
        or change anything at the bank. It has no ability to do so, by design.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the data is stored</h2>
      <p>
        Everything the application retrieves is written to a local database file on my own computer.
        It is not uploaded to a server, not synced to cloud storage, and not backed up anywhere
        off-device. There is no hosted component to this application — no website, no API, no
        database that I or anyone else operates remotely.
      </p>
      <p>
        The credentials used to authenticate with Enable Banking, including the private signing key,
        are stored in the same local folder with owner-only file permissions, and are excluded from
        version control so they cannot be published with the source code.
      </p>

      <h2>Who the data is shared with</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody. The data is not sold, not shared, not sent to advertisers, and not used to train
        anything. The application contains no analytics, no telemetry, and no third-party trackers.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only parties involved in the flow at all are my bank, which holds the account, and Enable
        Banking, which acts as the regulated intermediary that carries the data from the bank to my
        computer. Enable Banking processes that data under its own privacy policy and its licence as
        an account information service provider. No other processor is involved.
      </p>

      <h2>Consent, and how it ends</h2>
      <p>
        Access is granted through my bank's own authorisation screen, using the bank's own
        credentials. The application never sees or stores bank login details.
      </p>
      <p>
        That consent is time-limited under PSD2 — typically 90 to 180 days — after which access stops
        automatically unless it is renewed through the same authorisation flow. Consent can also be
        withdrawn at any time, immediately, from within online banking, without involving this
        application at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Transaction data stays in the local database until I delete it. The application includes a
        function that erases the entire local store in one action. Deleting the application's data
        folder has the same effect. Because nothing is stored remotely, deletion is final — there is
        no copy elsewhere to be removed.
      </p>

      <h2>Rights</h2>
      <p>
        I am the sole data subject and the sole operator, so the usual rights of access, correction,
        portability and erasure are exercised directly: the data is on my machine, in an open format,
        and I can read, export or destroy it at will. Rights against my bank and against Enable
        Banking are exercised through their respective processes.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If what the application does with data changes materially, this page is updated and the date
        at the top changes with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Belal Zaky — <a href="mailto:belal4606@gmail.com">belal4606@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-title {
      font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    }
  }

  .legal-dek {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 55ch;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
